:dart: Infosys – DevOps Interview Experience
Sharing a set of DevOps interview questions gathered from an external source. We believe these questions can be helpful for our students and DevOps professionals preparing for technical interviews.
The interview reportedly began with a self-introduction, followed by project-based and scenario-driven discussions focused on the technologies mentioned in the candidate's resume.

Interview Questions:
• How would you approach migrating a monolithic application to a microservices architecture? What steps would you follow, and what challenges would you expect during the migration?
• After deploying an application, users report performance degradation. How would you troubleshoot the issue and identify the root cause?
• What happens if a Terraform state file stored in an Amazon S3 bucket is accidentally deleted? How would you recover it, and what measures would you implement to prevent such incidents?
• What Jenkins strategy and pipeline type did you use in your project?
• Which Kubernetes deployment strategy did you implement, and why was it chosen?
• What is Immutable Infrastructure in Terraform? How does Terraform support this concept?
• Do you use a single CI/CD pipeline for Development, SIT, UAT, and Production environments, or separate pipelines? How do you manage environment-specific configurations and deployments?

Key Takeaway:
Your self-introduction often sets the direction of the interview. Be prepared to discuss every technology, tool, and project mentioned in your resume with practical implementation details, real-world use cases, and troubleshooting scenarios.

Hope this helps those preparing for DevOps interviews. Wishing everyone success in their preparation and upcoming opportunities.





