:rocket: Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions | 5+ Years Experience
Technical knowledge is essential, but for 5+ years of DevOps experience, interviewers expect you to demonstrate real-world production troubleshooting, decision-making, and incident management skills.
Here are some of the most frequently asked scenario-based interview questions:
:small_blue_diamond: Kubernetes

• A Kubernetes pod is stuck in CrashLoopBackOff. How would you troubleshoot it?.
• A Kubernetes deployment shows ImagePullBackOff. What checks would you perform?.
• Nodes in a Kubernetes cluster are running out of memory. How would you diagnose and resolve the issue?.
• A service becomes inaccessible after an Ingress update. What components would you verify?.
:small_blue_diamond: Deployments & CI/CD

• Your application is experiencing high latency after a new deployment. What steps would you take?.
• A production deployment failed halfway through. How would you perform a rollback while minimizing downtime?.
• Your CI/CD pipeline suddenly starts failing without any code changes. Where would you begin your investigation?.
• A database migration fails during deployment. What would your recovery plan be?.
:small_blue_diamond: Docker & Applications

• A Docker image works locally but fails in production. How would you identify the root cause?.
• An application cannot communicate with another microservice. How would you troubleshoot the issue?.
:small_blue_diamond: Monitoring & Security

• Monitoring alerts indicate high CPU usage across multiple pods. How would you investigate?.
• SSL certificates have expired in production. How would you renew and validate them safely?.
• Secrets need to be rotated without causing application downtime. How would you approach it?.
:small_blue_diamond: Cloud & Cost Optimization

• A cloud resource is causing unexpected costs. How would you identify and optimize it?.
:small_blue_diamond: Production Incident Management

• A production incident occurs at 2:00 AM. How would you lead the troubleshooting process and communicate with stakeholders?.
:bulb: Remember: Interviewers are not just looking for the correct answer—they want to understand your troubleshooting methodology, production experience, communication skills, and ability to handle critical incidents under pressure.
